{"id":22,"uuid":"43905534304367455094358729118296","menutype_id":null,"slug":"mattress-buying-guide","pagetype":1,"always_display":0,"sort_order":1,"status":1,"pagestyle":"null","pagescript":"null","deleted_at":null,"created_at":"2026-05-29T21:58:41.000000Z","updated_at":"2026-06-07T16:31:33.000000Z","global_options":"{\"siteName\": \"Site Name\", \"siteWidth\": \"1700px\", \"layoutType\": \"wide\", \"defaultFont\": \"Arial, sans-serif\", \"primaryColor\": \"#007bff\", \"secondaryColor\": \"#6c757d\"}","page_languages":[{"id":22,"page_id":"43905534304367455094358729118296","language_id":"d7f9d24a5f714f50d26a0d095799611c","title":"Mattress Buying Guide","is_advanced":0,"description":null,"long_description":"<!-- B3 MASTER FILE \u2014 Mattress Buying Guide (v2.2)\r\n     Reusable template. Swap demo data (\"South Jackson Furniture &amp; Mattress\", (731) 423-6565, southjacksonfurniture.com, Jackson)\r\n     and the CSS color variables for the retailer's style guide. Backgrounds are full-bleed (100vw) per v2.2.\r\n     META TITLE (plain text): Mattress Buying Guide | South Jackson Furniture &amp; Mattress\r\n     META DESCRIPTION (plain text): How to choose a mattress \u2014 compare innerspring, memory foam, hybrid, and latex; pick firmness and size; and find the best mattress for your sleep style. -->\r\n<link href=\"https:\/\/fonts.googleapis.com\/css2?family=Montserrat:wght@400;500;600;700;800;900&amp;family=Inter:ital,wght@0,400;0,700;1,400&amp;display=swap\" rel=\"stylesheet\">\r\n<style>\r\n .b3mbg{--maxw:1180px;--pad:clamp(24px,5vw,50px);\r\n  --navy:#AE1F1A;--navyd:#AE1F1A;--navyt:#E8F4FB;--brick:#FFE000;--brickd:#0C5E96;\r\n  --blush:#FFE000;--ink:#1A1A1A;--slate:#3A3A3A;--line:#E4E2DE;--mist:#F7F6F4;--band:#F7F6F4;\r\n  --display:'Montserrat',-apple-system,sans-serif;--body:'Inter',-apple-system,sans-serif;\r\n  font-family:var(--body);color:var(--ink);line-height:1.7;font-size:17px;-webkit-font-smoothing:antialiased;}\r\n .b3mbg *,.b3mbg *::before,.b3mbg *::after{box-sizing:border-box;}\r\n .b3mbg p{margin:0 1em;} .b3mbg a{color:var(--navy);font-weight:700;text-decoration:none;}\r\n .b3mbg h1,.b3mbg h2,.b3mbg h3,.b3mbg h4,.b3mbg .eyebrow,.b3mbg summary,.b3mbg .num,.b3mbg th,.b3mbg .stat-n{font-family:var(--display);}\r\n .b3mbg-wrap{max-width:var(--maxw);margin:0 auto;padding:0 var(--pad);}\r\n .b3mbg-band{width:100vw;position:relative;left:50%;right:50%;margin-left:-50vw;margin-right:-50vw;}\r\n .b3mbg-section{padding:72px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);}\r\n .b3mbg-section:last-child{border-bottom:none;}\r\n .b3mbg-shead{margin-bottom:38px;padding-left:20px;border-left:4px solid var(--brick);}\r\n .b3mbg .eyebrow{font-size:11px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brick);margin:0 8px;}\r\n .b3mbg-shead h2{font-size:clamp(26px,3.4vw,38px);font-weight:800;color:var(--navy);margin:0;letter-spacing:-.6px;line-height:1.12;}\r\n .b3mbg h2,.b3mbg h3{font-weight:800;color:var(--navy);}\r\n .b3mbg-section p{font-size:17px;color:#3A3A3A;}\r\n .b3mbg strong{color:var(--ink);font-weight:700;}\r\n \/* HERO *\/\r\n .b3mbg-hero{background:var(--navy);color:#fff;padding:84px 0;position:relative;overflow:hidden;border-bottom:6px solid var(--brick);}\r\n .b3mbg-hero::before{content:\"\";position:absolute;top:-25%;right:-8%;width:620px;height:620px;background:radial-gradient(circle,rgba(255,224,0,.30)0%,transparent 68%);pointer-events:none;}\r\n .b3mbg-hero .b3mbg-wrap{position:relative;}\r\n .b3mbg-hero .eyebrow{color:var(--blush);font-size:12px;letter-spacing:3px;}\r\n .b3mbg-hero h1{font-size:clamp(36px,5.2vw,58px);font-weight:800;line-height:1.04;color:#fff;margin:0 20px;letter-spacing:-1.1px;}\r\n .b3mbg-hero h1 .accent{color:var(--blush);}\r\n .b3mbg-hero p{font-size:19px;color:rgba(255,255,255,.9);margin:0;max-width:62ch;}\r\n .b3mbg-tagline{display:inline-block;font-family:var(--display);font-weight:700;font-size:16px;letter-spacing:1px;color:#fff;border-left:4px solid var(--brick);padding-left:16px;margin-top:28px;}\r\n \/* QUICK ANSWER (AEO) *\/\r\n .b3mbg-qa{background:var(--navyt);border-left:5px solid var(--brick);padding:26px 30px;margin:0 8px;}\r\n .b3mbg-qa .lab{font-family:var(--display);font-weight:700;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brick);margin:0 8px;}\r\n .b3mbg-qa p{font-size:18px;color:var(--ink);margin:0;line-height:1.65;}\r\n \/* PILLARS *\/\r\n .b3mbg-pillars{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:18px;}\r\n @media(max-width:900px){.b3mbg-pillars{grid-template-columns:1fr;}}\r\n .b3mbg-pillar{background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:4px;padding:26px;}\r\n .b3mbg-pillar .num{width:40px;height:40px;background:var(--navy);color:#fff;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:800;border-radius:4px;margin-bottom:14px;}\r\n .b3mbg-pillar h3{font-size:18px;margin:0 6px;} .b3mbg-pillar p{font-size:15px;color:var(--slate);margin:0;}\r\n \/* OFFER GRID *\/\r\n .b3mbg-grid3{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:18px;}\r\n @media(max-width:900px){.b3mbg-grid3{grid-template-columns:1fr;}}\r\n .b3mbg-card{background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:4px;padding:28px;}\r\n .b3mbg-card h4{font-size:17px;color:var(--navy);margin:0 8px;font-weight:700;font-family:var(--display);}\r\n .b3mbg-card p{font-size:15px;color:var(--slate);margin:0;}\r\n \/* STAT BAND *\/\r\n .b3mbg-stats{background:var(--navyd);color:#fff;}\r\n .b3mbg-stats .b3mbg-wrap{padding-top:48px;padding-bottom:48px;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:20px;text-align:center;}\r\n @media(max-width:760px){.b3mbg-stats .b3mbg-wrap{grid-template-columns:1fr;}}\r\n .b3mbg-stat .stat-n{font-size:34px;font-weight:800;color:var(--blush);}\r\n .b3mbg-stat .stat-l{font-size:13px;letter-spacing:1px;text-transform:uppercase;color:rgba(255,255,255,.8);font-family:var(--display);font-weight:600;}\r\n \/* LOCATIONS *\/\r\n .b3mbg-locs{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:22px;}\r\n @media(max-width:820px){.b3mbg-locs{grid-template-columns:1fr;}}\r\n .b3mbg-loc{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;border-top:5px solid var(--navy);padding:30px;}\r\n .b3mbg-loc .tag{font-family:var(--display);font-weight:700;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--brick);margin-bottom:10px;}\r\n .b3mbg-loc h3{font-size:20px;margin:0 6px;} .b3mbg-loc p{font-size:15px;color:var(--slate);margin:0 5px;}\r\n .b3mbg-map{width:100%;height:240px;border:0;border-radius:4px;margin-top:14px;}\r\n \/* TABLE *\/\r\n .b3mbg-table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;border:1px solid var(--line);margin-top:8px;}\r\n .b3mbg-table th{background:var(--navy);color:#fff;text-align:left;padding:13px 16px;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:1px;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:700;}\r\n .b3mbg-table td{padding:12px 16px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);font-size:15px;color:#3A3A3A;}\r\n .b3mbg-table td:first-child{font-family:var(--display);font-weight:700;color:var(--ink);}\r\n .b3mbg-table tr:last-child td{border-bottom:none;}\r\n \/* FIRMNESS *\/\r\n .b3mbg-firm{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:16px;}\r\n @media(max-width:760px){.b3mbg-firm{grid-template-columns:1fr;}}\r\n .b3mbg-firm-card{background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:4px;padding:24px;text-align:center;}\r\n .b3mbg-firm-card .lvl{font-family:var(--display);font-weight:800;font-size:17px;color:var(--navy);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.5px;margin-bottom:10px;}\r\n .b3mbg-firm-card p{font-size:14px;color:var(--slate);margin:0;}\r\n \/* TYPE CARD *\/\r\n .b3mbg-type{background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--line);border-left:5px solid var(--navy);border-radius:4px;padding:26px 30px;margin-bottom:16px;}\r\n .b3mbg-type h3{font-size:20px;margin:0 8px;} .b3mbg-type p{margin:0 10px;color:#3A3A3A;}\r\n .b3mbg-best{display:inline-block;background:var(--mist);color:var(--navy);font-family:var(--display);font-weight:600;font-size:13px;padding:7px 13px;border-radius:4px;border-left:3px solid var(--brick);}\r\n \/* JUMP NAV *\/\r\n .b3mbg-jump{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px;margin-top:6px;}\r\n .b3mbg-jump a{font-family:var(--display);font-weight:700;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.5px;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--navy);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:4px;padding:9px 14px;}\r\n .b3mbg-jump a:hover{border-color:var(--navy);background:var(--navyt);}\r\n \/* FAQ *\/\r\n .b3mbg-fgroup{margin-bottom:30px;} .b3mbg-fgroup>h2{font-size:20px;color:var(--navy);margin:0 14px;padding-bottom:10px;border-bottom:2px solid var(--line);}\r\n .b3mbg-faq-item{background:#fff;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:4px;margin-bottom:10px;}\r\n .b3mbg-faq-item[open]{border-color:var(--navy);box-shadow:0 8px 22px rgba(46,45,107,.10);}\r\n .b3mbg-faq-item summary{font-size:16px;font-weight:700;color:var(--ink);padding:18px 24px;cursor:pointer;list-style:none;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:18px;align-items:center;}\r\n .b3mbg-faq-item summary::-webkit-details-marker{display:none;}\r\n .b3mbg-faq-item summary::after{content:\"+\";font-size:24px;font-weight:300;color:var(--brick);}\r\n .b3mbg-faq-item[open] summary::after{content:\"\\2212\";}\r\n .b3mbg-faq-a{padding:2px 24px 20px;font-size:15.5px;line-height:1.7;color:var(--slate);}\r\n \/* BUTTONS *\/\r\n .b3mbg a.b3mbg-btn,.b3mbg .b3mbg-btn{display:inline-block;font-family:var(--display);font-weight:700;font-size:14px;letter-spacing:.4px;padding:14px 28px;border-radius:4px;text-decoration:none;border:2px solid var(--navy);background:var(--navy);color:#fff;}\r\n .b3mbg a.b3mbg-btn:hover,.b3mbg .b3mbg-btn:hover{background:var(--navyd);border-color:var(--navyd);color:#fff;}\r\n .b3mbg a.b3mbg-btn-brick,.b3mbg .b3mbg-btn-brick{background:var(--brick);border-color:var(--brick);color:#fff;} .b3mbg a.b3mbg-btn-brick:hover{background:var(--brickd);border-color:var(--brickd);color:#fff;}\r\n .b3mbg a.b3mbg-btn-ghost,.b3mbg .b3mbg-btn-ghost{background:transparent;color:#fff;border-color:rgba(255,255,255,.6);} .b3mbg a.b3mbg-btn-ghost:hover{background:rgba(255,255,255,.12);color:#fff;}\r\n \/* CTA *\/\r\n .b3mbg-cta{background:var(--brick);color:#fff;text-align:center;}\r\n .b3mbg-cta .b3mbg-wrap{padding-top:64px;padding-bottom:64px;}\r\n .b3mbg-cta h2{color:#fff;font-size:clamp(24px,3vw,34px);margin:0 12px;}\r\n .b3mbg-cta p{color:rgba(255,255,255,.92);max-width:60ch;margin:0 auto 24px;}\r\n .b3mbg-cta-btns{display:flex;gap:14px;justify-content:center;flex-wrap:wrap;}\r\n .b3mbg-cta a.b3mbg-btn{border-color:#fff;background:#fff;color:var(--brick);}\r\n .b3mbg-cta a.b3mbg-btn:hover{background:var(--navyt);color:var(--brick);}\r\n .b3mbg-cta a.b3mbg-btn-ghost{background:transparent;color:#fff;border-color:rgba(255,255,255,.7);}\r\n .b3mbg-updated{font-size:13px;color:var(--slate);margin-top:22px;font-style:italic;}\r\n<\/style>\r\n<div class=\"b3mbg\">\r\n  <section class=\"b3mbg-band b3mbg-hero\"><div class=\"b3mbg-wrap\">\r\n    <div class=\"eyebrow\">Mattress Buying Guide<\/div>\r\n    <h1>Find the <span class=\"accent\">perfect mattress<\/span><\/h1>\r\n    <p>Compare mattress types, choose the right firmness and size for your sleep style, and shop trusted brands \u2014 all at South Jackson Furniture &amp; Mattress's everyday low prices.<\/p>\r\n  <\/div><\/section>\r\n\r\n  <div class=\"b3mbg-wrap\"><section class=\"b3mbg-section\">\r\n    <div class=\"b3mbg-qa\"><div class=\"lab\">Quick Answer<\/div>\r\n      <p>The best mattress depends on your <strong>sleep position<\/strong> and <strong>preferred feel<\/strong>. Side sleepers do best on soft\u2013medium <strong>memory foam<\/strong>; back and stomach sleepers on medium\u2013firm <strong>hybrid or innerspring<\/strong>. Queen is the most popular size for couples. Try them in person at our showroom, or call <a href=\"tel:2155550199\">(731) 423-6565<\/a>.<\/p><\/div>\r\n  <\/section><\/div>\r\n\r\n  <div class=\"b3mbg-wrap\"><section class=\"b3mbg-section\">\r\n    <div class=\"b3mbg-shead\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">Know Your Options<\/div><h2>Mattress types explained<\/h2><\/div>\r\n    <div class=\"b3mbg-type\"><h3>Innerspring Mattresses<\/h3><p>Innerspring mattresses use a system of steel coils for support. They're the most traditional type, with a firmer feel, good bounce, and excellent airflow.<\/p><span class=\"b3mbg-best\">Best for: responsive sleep &amp; people who sleep hot<\/span><\/div>\r\n    <div class=\"b3mbg-type\"><h3>Memory Foam Mattresses<\/h3><p>Memory foam contours to your body, providing targeted pressure relief for shoulders, hips, and back. It absorbs motion well, making it great for couples.<\/p><span class=\"b3mbg-best\">Best for: side sleepers, joint pain &amp; a contouring feel<\/span><\/div>\r\n    <div class=\"b3mbg-type\"><h3>Hybrid Mattresses<\/h3><p>Hybrids combine an innerspring coil base with foam comfort layers \u2014 the support and airflow of coils with the pressure relief of foam.<\/p><span class=\"b3mbg-best\">Best for: balanced support, back &amp; combination sleepers<\/span><\/div>\r\n    <div class=\"b3mbg-type\"><h3>Adjustable Bases<\/h3><p>An adjustable base raises the head and\/or foot of your mattress to help with snoring, acid reflux, circulation, and reading in bed. Most foam and hybrid mattresses pair well with one.<\/p><span class=\"b3mbg-best\">Best for: custom positioning &amp; added comfort<\/span><\/div>\r\n  <\/section><\/div>\r\n\r\n  <div class=\"b3mbg-band\" style=\"background:var(--mist);\"><div class=\"b3mbg-wrap\"><section class=\"b3mbg-section\" style=\"border-bottom:none;\">\r\n    <div class=\"b3mbg-shead\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">Compare at a Glance<\/div><h2>Which mattress type is right for you?<\/h2><\/div>\r\n    <table class=\"b3mbg-table\">\r\n      <thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Feel<\/th><th>Best For<\/th><\/tr><\/thead>\r\n      <tbody>\r\n        <tr><td>Innerspring<\/td><td>Firm, bouncy, cool<\/td><td>Hot sleepers, classic support<\/td><\/tr>\r\n        <tr><td>Memory Foam<\/td><td>Contouring, plush<\/td><td>Side sleepers, joint &amp; pressure relief<\/td><\/tr>\r\n        <tr><td>Hybrid<\/td><td>Balanced support + relief<\/td><td>Back &amp; combination sleepers, couples<\/td><\/tr>\r\n      <\/tbody>\r\n    <\/table>\r\n  <\/section><\/div><\/div>\r\n\r\n  <div class=\"b3mbg-wrap\"><section class=\"b3mbg-section\">\r\n    <div class=\"b3mbg-shead\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">Find Your Feel<\/div><h2>Choosing the right firmness<\/h2><\/div>\r\n    <p>Firmness is personal \u2014 the best way to find yours is to try mattresses in person at our showroom. As a starting point:<\/p>\r\n    <div class=\"b3mbg-firm\">\r\n      <div class=\"b3mbg-firm-card\"><div class=\"lvl\">Soft<\/div><p>Best for side sleepers and lighter individuals \u2014 lets shoulders and hips sink in for pressure relief.<\/p><\/div>\r\n      <div class=\"b3mbg-firm-card\"><div class=\"lvl\">Medium<\/div><p>Works for most sleepers and positions. The most popular choice for a balance of support and comfort.<\/p><\/div>\r\n      <div class=\"b3mbg-firm-card\"><div class=\"lvl\">Firm<\/div><p>Best for stomach and back sleepers and heavier individuals \u2014 keeps the spine in neutral alignment.<\/p><\/div>\r\n    <\/div>\r\n  <\/section><\/div>\r\n\r\n  <div class=\"b3mbg-wrap\"><section class=\"b3mbg-section\">\r\n    <div class=\"b3mbg-shead\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">Size It Right<\/div><h2>Which mattress size should you get?<\/h2><\/div>\r\n    <table class=\"b3mbg-table\">\r\n      <thead><tr><th>Size<\/th><th>Best For<\/th><\/tr><\/thead>\r\n      <tbody>\r\n        <tr><td>Twin \/ Twin XL<\/td><td>Children, teens, and single sleepers in smaller rooms<\/td><\/tr>\r\n        <tr><td>Full<\/td><td>Single adults who want more room in a compact space<\/td><\/tr>\r\n        <tr><td>Queen<\/td><td>The most popular size for couples<\/td><\/tr>\r\n        <tr><td>King<\/td><td>Couples who want extra space, or who share with kids and pets<\/td><\/tr>\r\n      <\/tbody>\r\n    <\/table>\r\n  <\/section><\/div>\r\n\r\n  <div class=\"b3mbg-wrap\"><section class=\"b3mbg-section\">\r\n    <div class=\"b3mbg-shead\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">Step by Step<\/div><h2>How to choose a mattress<\/h2><\/div>\r\n    <table class=\"b3mbg-table\"><tbody><tr><td>Step 1<\/td><td><strong>Pick your mattress type.<\/strong> Decide between innerspring, memory foam, or hybrid based on the feel you want \u2014 bouncy and cool, contouring and pressure-relieving, or a balance of both.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Step 2<\/td><td><strong>Choose your firmness.<\/strong> Match firmness to your sleep position: soft for side sleepers, medium for most people, firm for stomach and back sleepers.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Step 3<\/td><td><strong>Select the right size.<\/strong> Choose Twin, Full, Queen, or King based on your room size and who shares the bed.<\/td><\/tr><tr><td>Step 4<\/td><td><strong>Try it in the showroom.<\/strong> Visit South Jackson Furniture &amp; Mattress in our showroom to lie on each option and let our team match you to the right mattress.<\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table>\r\n  <\/section><\/div>\r\n\r\n  <div class=\"b3mbg-wrap\"><section class=\"b3mbg-section\">\r\n    <div class=\"b3mbg-shead\"><div class=\"eyebrow\">Good to Know<\/div><h2>Common mattress questions<\/h2><\/div>\r\n        <details class=\"b3mbg-faq-item\"><summary>How often should I replace my mattress?<\/summary><div class=\"b3mbg-faq-a\">Most mattresses last 7 to 10 years depending on quality, usage, and care. If you're waking up with aches and pains, notice visible sagging, or your mattress is over 8 years old, it's probably time for an upgrade.<\/div><\/details>\r\n        <details class=\"b3mbg-faq-item\"><summary>Do I need a box spring?<\/summary><div class=\"b3mbg-faq-a\">It depends on the mattress and your bed frame. Many modern mattresses work with platform beds, adjustable bases, or slatted frames without a traditional box spring. Check your mattress warranty for base requirements.<\/div><\/details>\r\n        <details class=\"b3mbg-faq-item\"><summary>What mattress size should I get?<\/summary><div class=\"b3mbg-faq-a\">Consider your room size, how many people will use the bed, and whether you share with a partner or pets. Queen is the most popular for couples. King gives extra space. Full works for single adults in smaller rooms. Twin and Twin XL are ideal for children and teens.<\/div><\/details>\r\n        <details class=\"b3mbg-faq-item\"><summary>Which mattress type is best for side sleepers?<\/summary><div class=\"b3mbg-faq-a\">Memory foam mattresses are an excellent choice for side sleepers because they contour to the body and provide targeted pressure relief for the shoulders and hips. A soft to medium firmness usually works best for side sleepers.<\/div><\/details>\r\n        <details class=\"b3mbg-faq-item\"><summary>What is the best mattress firmness?<\/summary><div class=\"b3mbg-faq-a\">Firmness is personal. Soft mattresses suit side sleepers and lighter individuals. Medium works for most sleepers and positions and is the most popular choice. Firm mattresses suit stomach and back sleepers and heavier individuals, keeping the spine in neutral alignment.<\/div><\/details>\r\n        <details class=\"b3mbg-faq-item\"><summary>Which mattress is best for back pain?<\/summary><div class=\"b3mbg-faq-a\">For back pain, look for a medium-firm mattress that keeps your spine in neutral alignment. Memory foam and hybrid mattresses both relieve pressure while supporting the lower back. The best way to be sure is to try a few in our showroom.<\/div><\/details>\r\n  <\/section><\/div>\r\n\r\n  <section class=\"b3mbg-band b3mbg-cta\"><div class=\"b3mbg-wrap\">\r\n    <h2>A great night starts here<\/h2>\r\n    <p>Try our mattresses in person and let our local team match you to the right feel. Where the prices are low.<\/p>\r\n    <div class=\"b3mbg-cta-btns\">\r\n      <a class=\"b3mbg-btn\" href=\"https:\/\/southjacksonfurniture.com\/collections\/mattress\">Shop Mattresses<\/a>\r\n      <a class=\"b3mbg-btn b3mbg-btn-ghost\" href=\"https:\/\/southjacksonfurniture.com\/pages\/financing\">View Financing<\/a>\r\n    <\/div>\r\n  <\/div><\/section>\r\n<\/div>","builder_data":null,"builder_page_option":null,"meta_title":"Mattress Buying Guide","meta_description":"Mattress Buying Guide","meta_keyword":"Mattress Buying Guide","created_at":"2026-05-29T21:58:41.000000Z","updated_at":"2026-06-07T16:31:33.000000Z"}],"menutype":null}